    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-114406",
      "kind": "accepted-risk-upstream-package",
      "reason": "Re-accepted by the owner on 2026-11-04 for the 2026-11-13 CentOS Stream 10 base. Red Hat's tracker for removing the compromised eMudhra roots (RHSB-2026-012) from ca-certificates. The base serves 2026.2.92_v9.0.319-100.3: its changelog removes emSign Root CA - C1 (100.0), AAA Certificate Services and emSign ECC Root CA - G3 (100.1), and emSign Root CS CA - G3 (100.2), and the extracted bundle has no eMudhra root. Grype still matches this CVE against 100.3 because its database has not caught up; this entry documents that false positive until it does. Scope: the system trust store. Browsers keep their own store, which the root programs already fixed. Drop this entry when a scan stops reporting the CVE. Matches re-read from the 2026-11-13 base scan on 2026-11-24; the acceptance stands.",
      "matches": [
        {
          "package": "ca-certificates",
          "type": "rpm",
          "version": "2026.2.92_v9.0.319-100.3.el10",
          "path": "/usr/share/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-115905",
      "kind": "accepted-risk-upstream-package",
      "reason": "Accepted by the owner on 2026-11-04 for the 2026-11-13 CentOS Stream 10 base. Red Hat rates the CVE Critical (CVSS 3.1 8.1, draft), records RHEL 10 firefox as Affected and publishes no fixed build: the flaw is in the zip streaming extractor, the package is the vendor's, and DeskOS neither builds nor patches it. Blocking the fleet would not reduce the risk; the fix is Red Hat's rebuild in a later base. The tracked issue is #420, and the base bump that carries it closes the entry. This record makes the acceptance explicit and expires on the review date below. Matches re-read from the 2026-11-13 base scan on 2026-11-24; the acceptance stands.",
      "matches": [
        {
